diff --git a/packages/client/ui-sidebar-browser/README.md b/packages/client/ui-sidebar-browser/README.md
index e3664ef582d6fa980a40a9e7679c0e8b4b34d0f6..946455781deec1f40736dffd44e789e31026f456 100644
--- a/packages/client/ui-sidebar-browser/README.md
+++ b/packages/client/ui-sidebar-browser/README.md
@@ -27,6 +27,8 @@ Browse HTTP(S) pages, including loopback services, inside independent right-Side
 
 Browser is disabled by default in Web profiles and enabled on Desktop. Enable the shipped entry through the Web profile patch to use it. Open **Browser** from the right-Sidebar guide and enter an HTTP(S) URL. Chat HTTP(S) links open here when the [link preference](../ui-chat/README.md) selects **In-App Sidebar**. A host name without a scheme becomes HTTPS. Public and loopback targets use the same default sandbox. Each guide action or delegated message-link activation creates another Browser tab.
 
+The same Client plugin registers the root-scoped `browser.content` factory for an independent browser graph. Render it with `{ url }`; no Session, Workspace, Sidebar service or persisted store is required. Each occurrence reuses the native Browser chrome and controller and releases its page on unmount. Web always applies `sandbox="allow-scripts allow-forms"`, retaining an opaque origin with no popup, top-navigation or sandbox-lowering control. `credentialless` is an additional browser hint, not the isolation guarantee. Desktop creates a fresh opaque, process-local storage identity for each occurrence instead of resolving a local Workspace. Only the toolbar's explicit external-open action launches another browser. Existing Sidebar tabs retain their prior behavior.
+
 ### When to choose it
 
 Choose Browser for a Web page that should remain beside the current Session. Choose [Document Preview](../ui-sidebar-documentpreview/README.md) for local files, and use the explicit external-browser action when a site refuses iframe embedding or needs browser capabilities this package withholds.
